<section class="container section-pad"><div class="section-head"><span class="eyebrow">KNOW WHAT YOU’RE HIRING FOR</span><h2>A working relationship with clear priorities</h2><p>Tell us about your business before choosing a program. We confirm your goals, responsibilities and deliverables in a proposal.</p></div><div class="grid grid-3"><article class="card"><h3>What to share with us</h3><p>Your website, main services, target cities or countries, current challenges and business goals. If you have previous SEO reports, mention them in your enquiry.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>What we plan together</h3><p>The initial audit, keyword priorities, technical fixes, page improvements and content direction. The agreed proposal sets the scope and clarifies which changes your team will implement.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>How progress is reviewed</h3><p>Review completed tasks, audit findings and available performance data. Monthly reporting helps you understand the work completed and priorities for the next period.</p></article></div><div class="expert-faq"><h2>Before you hire an SEO expert</h2><details><summary>Is a workspace plan the same as an SEO expert program?</summary><p>No. Workspace plans provide access to tools and their listed limits. Expert programs are managed services with a separate scope and program price.</p></details><details><summary>Will you guarantee a first-page ranking?</summary><p>No. Search positions depend on your website, competition, content and search engine decisions. We focus on agreed work, useful recommendations and transparent reporting.</p></details><details><summary>What happens after I submit an enquiry?</summary><p>The team reviews your website and goals, discusses the service scope and confirms a proposal. Submitting an enquiry does not charge you or start a paid program.</p></details><details><summary>Can you help a local business?</summary><p>Yes, you can request a local SEO assessment. Include the cities you serve and your business profile details so the team can discuss the right scope.</p></details></div></section>
